  "imagery": "The site is text- and code-dominant, not photography-led. The primary visual is the embedded TypeScript code editor (Ink Well background, multi-color syntax highlighting) which functions as both product demonstration and decorative asset. Feature pills at the page footer use small chromatic icons (2-3px stroke, filled style) in violet, pink, green, and yellow to create color rhythm without imagery. Customer testimonials include small circular avatars and grayscale company logos rendered in a uniform row. There is no lifestyle photography, no hero illustration, no 3D rendering — the visual weight comes from type hierarchy, code blocks, and the lime accent. The overall density is text-forward: code and copy do the work that images would do on a consumer product site.",
